	(footprint "robot-projects:SparkFun_TB6612FNG_v2"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "adc5e0f9-e35b-48b5-b6b6-4021bcce1eb4")
		(at 34.9 17.4 180)
		(descr "SparkFun Motor Driver - Dual TB6612FNG v2 (w/ Headers). Through-hole female socket for breakout board. 2x8 pins, 2.54mm pitch, 15.24mm row spacing and 20.32x20.32mm body BOTH confirmed from the vendor Eagle SparkFun_Motor_Driver-TB6612FNG_v11c.brd: layer 20 (Dimension) is a 0..20.32 square, JP1 at (2.54,1.27) R90 and JP2 at (17.78,19.05) R270. Body therefore extends 2.54mm beyond each pad column in X and 1.27mm beyond the end pads in Y. Do not re-derive by eye. PINOUT (chip up, top view, = the .brd): left column x -7.62 top->bottom VM VCC GND AO1 AO2 BO2 BO1 GND = pads 9-16 (JP1 pin 8->1); right column x +7.62 top->bottom PWMA AIN2 AIN1 STBY BIN1 BIN2 PWMB GND = pads 1-8 (JP2 pin 1->8). VM sits across from PWMA. Until 2026-11-09 the two columns were swapped, a MIRROR of the module (seating it shorted VM to GND): check handedness, not just pin order.")
